FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] src/formats.rs:509 — multiline basic strings accept a closing run of six or more delimiter quotes (and `src/formats.rs:548` does the same for multiline literal strings): `quote_run` counts the whole run, then `run >= 3` treats `run - 3` quotes as content and consumes all of them. TOML allows at most five consecutive quotes at the close (two content + three delimiter), so `x = """a""""""` silently parses as `a"""` instead of being refused as malformed. The fix is to error when `run > 5`; add a test for the six-quote case, which is untested on either side.
2. [MINOR] src/formats.rs:590 — `skip_line_continuation` includes a bare `'\r'` in its whitespace set and treats it as a line break even when it is not followed by `'\n'`, while `trim_leading_newline` (`src/formats.rs:576`) only trims `\r\n` or `\n`. A backslash followed by a lone CR is therefore silently treated as a continuation and that CR is dropped from the value, although TOML defines a newline only as LF or CRLF. Require `\n` or `\r\n` here (and decide whether a lone CR should instead be content/rejected), and add a test pinning it.

Both are malformed-input acceptance gaps in the newly added multiline TOML path; the actually valid cases (first-newline trimming, two-quote runs, CRLF, line continuation) are covered by `tests/data_formats_test.rs`.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 2
